# The volume signing key, mounted read-only at /secrets.
#
# NEVER COMMIT ANYTHING HERE. This is the key operators pin by `did:key` to decide whether they trust a
# volume; leaking it lets anyone publish places into their map, which signing exists to prevent
# (apps/atlas/doc/spec/beacon-integration.md §2 and §7).
#
# Create one with `cartographer keygen --file secrets/publisher.key` (apps/atlas/README.md, "Create
# the signing key"): a BIP39 recovery phrase written mode 600. Back it up somewhere that is not
# this directory.
#
# `publish` refuses a file with any group/world permission bit set, and refuses to run at all without
# one: there is no unsigned mode. The repository root's .gitignore ignores this directory too, so
# deleting this file does not open it.
*
!.gitignore
